data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">vegetable broth</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Base of the gravy</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">soy sauce or tamari</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds umami flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">nutritional yeast (optional)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds a cheesy flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">dried thyme</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Herb flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">dried sage</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Herb flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt and pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For seasoning</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-9158-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"9158\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Medium saucepan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the gravy</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-9158-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-9158-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"9158\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a medium saucepan, melt vegan butter or heat olive oil over medium heat.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Add the finely chopped onion and sauté for 4–5 minutes until translucent.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Stir in the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute more.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Sprinkle in the all-purpose flour and whisk constantly for 2 minutes to form a roux.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Gradually pour in the vegetable broth while whisking to prevent lumps.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Add soy sauce or tamari, nutritional yeast (if using), dried thyme, and dried sage.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bring the mixture to a gentle boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until thickened.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Season with salt and pepper to taste.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-9158-step-0-8\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Remove from heat and serve warm over mashed potatoes, roasted vegetables, or your favorite dishes.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-9158-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>100</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>12g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s what you&#8217;ll need to whip up a delicious vegan <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gravy</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Vegan-Gravy-Ingredients-Display.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for vegan gravy displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-9156\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Vegan-Gravy-Ingredients-Display.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Vegan-Gravy-Ingredients-Display-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons</strong> – vegan butter or olive oil</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 small</strong> – onion (finely chopped)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cloves</strong> – garlic (minced)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup</strong> – all-purpose flour</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cups</strong> – vegetable broth</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon</strong> – soy sauce or tamari</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon</strong> – nutritional yeast (optional)</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 teaspoon</strong> – dried thyme</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 teaspoon</strong> – dried sage</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>salt and pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-vegan-gravy\"><strong>How to Make Vegan Gravy</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful Vegan Gravy is quick to prepare, taking about 10 minutes, with a cooking time of 15 minutes. Perfect for drizzling over your favorite dishes!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Vegan-Gravy-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making vegan gravy, including melting vegan butter, sautéing onions, adding garlic, and making a roux.\" class=\"wp-image-9157\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Vegan-Gravy-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Step-by-Step-Vegan-Gravy-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Melt the Butter</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a medium saucepan, melt vegan butter or heat olive oil over medium heat.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Sauté the Onion</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the finely chopped onion and sauté for 4–5 minutes until translucent.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add Garlic</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir in the minced garlic and cook for 1 minute more.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Make the Roux</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sprinkle in the all-purpose flour and whisk constantly for 2 minutes to form a roux.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Add Broth</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gradually pour in the vegetable broth while whisking to prevent lumps.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Season the Gravy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add soy sauce or tamari, nutritional yeast (if using), dried thyme, and dried sage.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Simmer</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bring the mixture to a gentle boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until thickened.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Season to Taste</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season with salt and pepper to taste.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Serve Warm</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove from heat and serve warm over mashed potatoes, roasted vegetables, or your favorite dishes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Sauce</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Vegan</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegan</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm over mashed potatoes or roasted vegetables</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-vegan-gravy\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Vegan gravy</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use vegetable broth for a rich base.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add nutritional yeast for a cheesy flavor boost.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Incorporate miso paste for depth and umami.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Whisk continuously to avoid lumps and achieve creaminess.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust seasoning with soy sauce or tamari for extra flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-vegan-gravy\"><strong>How to Serve this Vegan gravy</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pour over fluffy mashed potatoes for a comforting classic.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle on roasted vegetables for added flavor and richness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a savory sauce for vegan meatloaf or lentil loaf.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside biscuits for a delightful brunch treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top your favorite grain bowl with a generous ladle of gravy.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with vegan shepherd&#8217;s pie for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a dipping sauce for crispy tofu or veggie nuggets.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to store your delicious vegan gravy for later use:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Vegan gravy Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow gravy to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Vegan gravy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or bags for storage.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Leave some space for expansion as it freezes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Vegan gravy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat on the stovetop over low heat, stirring frequently.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of vegetable broth for a smoother texture if needed.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How to make easy veggie gravy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Making easy veggie gravy is simple! Start by sautéing onions and garlic in a bit of olive oil until they&#8217;re soft. Then, add vegetable broth, soy sauce, and your favorite herbs and spices. Thicken it with a mixture of cornstarch and water, stirring until it reaches your desired consistency. This rich and flavorful gravy is perfect for drizzling over mashed potatoes or your favorite dishes!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Does Trader Joe&#8217;s have vegan gravy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Trader Joe&#8217;s offers a vegan gravy option! You can find it in the refrigerated section, and it&#8217;s a great convenience for those looking for a quick and tasty addition to their meals. Just check the label to ensure it meets your dietary preferences, and enjoy it over your favorite plant-based dishes!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the 3 2 1 rule for gravy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The 3 2 1 rule for gravy is a simple guideline for achieving the perfect consistency. It suggests using 3 parts liquid (like vegetable broth), 2 parts fat (such as olive oil or vegan butter), and 1 part thickener (like cornstarch or flour). This ratio helps create a smooth and rich gravy that complements any meal beautifully!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to try this easy, rich, and creamy vegan gravy as we are! It’s the perfect companion for your favorite dishes, bringing warmth and comfort to any meal. Remember, it’s simple to make and oh-so-rewarding. So grab your ingredients, get cooking, and enjoy every delicious bite!</p>\n",
